  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 1, 'Picture a home where you once felt welcome, and name one small thing the host did that put you at ease.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 2, 'Smile and say a warm hello to your host the moment the door opens, even before you take off your coat.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 3, 'Think of one small chore you enjoy, like drying dishes, so you have a ready offer at your next visit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 4, 'Before you pack, send your host a short note saying how much you are looking forward to the stay.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 5, 'Remember a goodbye that left you feeling warm, and think about what the person said.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 6, 'Reply to an invitation sitting in your messages today, even if your answer is simply "Yes, thank you, I would love to come."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 7, 'Hand your host anything you brought straight away, with a simple "This is for you."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 8, 'Ask your host "How can I help?" just once, and if they say no, thank them warmly and let it go.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 9, 'Ask your host what time the household usually wakes up so you can match its morning rhythm.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 10, 'Notice one gentle sign that a gathering is winding down, like the host stacking cups or a child yawning.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 11, 'Answer a party invitation within a day of getting it, so your host can plan with one less question in mind.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 12, 'Ask your host where they would like you to hang your coat on a winter evening, rather than draping it over a chair.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 13, 'Fill the water glasses on the table before everyone sits down to a family dinner, if your host is happy for you to.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 14, 'Find out the quiet hours on your first evening, then keep your voice and phone low after that time.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 15, 'Decide before an evening visit roughly when you''d like to head home, so leaving feels calm rather than sudden.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 16, 'Write a short, clear reply to a dinner invitation that says yes or no, thanks the host, and confirms the date.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 17, 'Spot one specific thing you like about the home, such as a lamp or a plant, and tell your host about it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 18, 'Carry a serving dish from the kitchen to the table when your host is juggling several at once.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 19, 'Fold your clothes into one neat pile in the guest room before you head down for breakfast.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 20, 'Glance at the clock after a summer barbecue and ask yourself whether your hosts might be ready for a quiet evening.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 21, 'Practice a kind way to decline out loud: "Thank you so much for thinking of me, I can''t make it this time."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 22, 'Greet everyone in the room at a family dinner, including the quiet cousin in the corner, with a simple hello and their name.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 23, 'Clear your own plate and cup after a meal and set them by the sink, unless your host waves you off.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 24, 'Make the bed each morning of your stay, even if the guest room door stays closed.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 25, 'Offer to carry plates to the kitchen before you put on your coat at the end of a family dinner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 26, 'Ask your host what time they would like you to arrive, rather than guessing at early or late.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 27, 'Let a dog sniff your closed hand before you reach to pet it, and only after the owner says it is fine.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 28, 'Practice a cheerful "That sounds lovely, thank you" for when a host turns down your offer of help.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 29, 'Keep your suitcase zipped and tucked against a wall so the guest space stays easy to walk through.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 30, 'Ask your host, "Can I help wash a few dishes before I go?" and accept a no with a smile.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 31, 'Text your host a simple question before a summer cookout: "Can I bring anything, or would you like me to come empty handed?"'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 32, 'Check with your host, "Is your cat friendly with visitors?" before you try to say hello to it.'),
