  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 40, 'Thank the youngest person at the gathering for showing you their drawing or toy before you leave.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 41, 'Check the invitation for an end time, and if there isn''t one, ask gently so you can plan the rest of your evening.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 42, 'Introduce yourself to one person you have not met at a backyard barbecue, and ask how they know the host.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 43, 'Sit beside an older relative at a holiday gathering and ask what winters were like when they were young.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 44, 'Offer to cook one simple dinner during a weekend stay, and let your host pick the night.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 45, 'Practice a short, warm goodbye line for the door, such as "This was lovely, thank you for having me."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 46, 'Mention a food allergy to your host when you reply, in one friendly sentence, rather than on the day itself.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 47, 'Wait for your host to show you where to sit at the table instead of choosing a seat yourself.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 48, 'Tell the cook one specific thing you enjoyed about the meal, such as the warmth of the soup or a spice you noticed.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 49, 'Pick up a few groceries the household uses often, such as milk, bread or fruit, on your way back from a walk.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 50, 'Keep your doorway goodbye to a minute or two, so your hosts are not standing in a cold draft on a winter night.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 51, 'Write one calm sentence you can use to share a food need: "I don''t eat dairy, but please don''t go to any trouble, I''ll find plenty."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 52, 'Put your phone in your bag or pocket as you walk through the door, and leave it there for the first hour.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 53, 'Steer a conversation gently away from gossip by asking about someone''s recent trip or hobby.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 54, 'Plan one afternoon out on your own so your host has a few quiet hours to themselves.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 55, 'Step outside with your coat already on once you''ve said goodbye, so the door conversation stays brief.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 56, 'Let your host know early if you hope to bring a child, partner or friend, and check first whether that suits them.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 57, 'Kneel down to a child''s eye level at a birthday party and say hello by name.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 58, 'Listen to a story at the table all the way through without glancing at your phone.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 59, 'Look up a museum, park or library near your host''s home and visit it alone for part of a day.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 60, 'Send a short thank you text to your host before you go to sleep tonight.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 61, 'Find out before a visit whether your host has pets, so you can plan around an allergy or simply look forward to saying hello.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 62, 'Thank your host for inviting you within the first minute of arriving at their place.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 63, 'Top up the pitcher of iced water at a summer barbecue when you see it running low.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 64, 'Wipe the bathroom sink and hang your towel neatly after your morning shower.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 65, 'Mention one specific dish, song or moment in your thank you message, like "That lemon cake was wonderful."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 66, 'Look up the route to a friend''s home tonight, so tomorrow''s trip feels familiar before you set out.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 67, 'Move with the rhythm your host sets: if they head to the living room, drift along with them.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 68, 'Hold the door for your host as they carry a tray out to the patio on a warm evening.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 69, 'Leave the thermostat where your host set it, and request an extra blanket if you feel cold.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 70, 'Write a short handwritten thank you note today to someone who hosted you recently.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 71, 'Plan how you''ll get home after an evening visit, whether that''s a bus time, a ride, or a friend heading the same way.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 72, 'Compliment the decorations at a kids'' birthday party by naming one detail, like the balloon arch or the handmade banner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 73, 'Invite your host''s child to show you a favorite toy, if their parent is glad of it, and listen as they tell you all about it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 74, 'On a winter holiday stay, bring warm socks and a sweater so you are cozy at the house''s usual temperature.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 75, 'Keep a few blank cards and stamps in a drawer so a thank you note is easy to send after any visit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 76, 'Save your host''s address and phone number in your phone before you leave, in case you need to call from the street.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 77, 'Check with your host which room the gathering will be in, so you do not wander through the house.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 78, 'Write down three easy questions to bring to your next visit, like "What has made you smile lately?"'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 79, 'Find out whether your host would like the sheets stripped on your last morning, then do as they prefer.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 80, 'Return a borrowed casserole dish within a few days, washed and dried, with a small note tucked inside.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 81, 'Check the bus or train times for a weekend visit and pick one that gets you there just before you''re expected.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 82, 'Offer to take off your shoes when you arrive, even if no one asks, and accept the answer either way.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 83, 'Bring in the folding chairs from the garage before a big family meal, if your host asks for a hand.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 84, 'Fold the stripped sheets and used towels into a tidy pile and ask where they should go.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 85, 'Put a borrowed container by your front door tonight so you remember to return it tomorrow.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 86, 'Find out where it is easiest to park near your host''s home, so you don''t block a neighbor''s driveway.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 87, 'Say hello to your host''s older relatives first when you arrive at a holiday gathering.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 88, 'Rinse your mug after morning coffee during a weekend stay and leave it on the drying rack.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 89, 'During a summer visit, check before opening windows or switching on a fan in the guest room.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 90, 'Invite a recent host to your place for a simple cup of tea or coffee.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 91, 'Allow a little extra travel time on a snowy winter evening, and let your host know if the roads slow you down.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 92, 'Learn the name of the host''s pet and use it when you greet them gently.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 93, 'Watch the oven timer or stir the pot while your host greets other guests at the door, if they would like that.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 94, 'Store your toiletries in your own bag rather than spreading them across a shared bathroom shelf.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 95, 'Suggest a walk in the park together as a way to return a friend''s hospitality if hosting at home feels like too much.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 96, 'Send a quick text if you''re running late, with a realistic new arrival time and a short sorry.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 97, 'Find out where the bathroom is by asking quietly when you arrive, so you are not hunting for it later.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 98, 'Settle onto the couch gracefully when your host insists you relax instead of helping.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 99, 'Wear headphones for any videos or music while others in the house are resting.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 100, 'Reflect for a minute on your way home about one moment of the visit that made you feel welcome.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 101, 'Pick up a small bunch of grocery store flowers on your way to a spring lunch, and keep the wrapping simple.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 102, 'Shake the rain from your umbrella on the step and ask where to leave it on a wet fall evening.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 103, 'Walk with the family around the block after a holiday dinner, keeping pace with the slowest walker.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 104, 'On a holiday stay with family, offer to take on one morning task, like setting the breakfast table.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 105, 'Let go of one small awkward moment from a visit by telling yourself, "Everyone has those, and it''s okay."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 106, 'Write a short card for your host that names one thing you are looking forward to about the visit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 107, 'Settle where your host points on the couch, and save rearranging the cushions for your own home.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 108, 'Point to a photo on the wall and invite an older guest to tell you the whole story behind it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 109, 'Rinse your own mug and plate after breakfast, then put them away the way your host likes.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 110, 'Plan a quiet hour at home after a busy holiday gathering, with a blanket, a book or a warm shower.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 111, 'Bake a small batch of cookies or muffins to bring along, and wrap them in a clean dish towel or a paper bag.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 112, 'Turn your phone to silent before you ring the doorbell at a friend''s apartment.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 113, 'Notice when someone at the table has been quiet, and ask them a gentle question to bring them in.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 114, 'Find out where the household keeps clean towels instead of guessing in closets.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 115, 'Leave the guest room bed neatly made or stripped, exactly as your host asked, on your last morning.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 116, 'Snip a cutting from one of your houseplants and set it in a jar of water, ready to give a host who loves green things.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 117, 'Breathe in the smell of something cooking as you arrive and tell your host it smells lovely.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 118, 'Say "This is delicious" out loud at the first bite of something you truly enjoy.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 119, 'Close the guest room door softly late at night so the sound does not carry down the hall.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 120, 'Sign your host''s guest book with a few warm words, if they keep one, before you leave.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 121, 'Pot a rooted plant cutting in a reused jar or cup, and tie on a string label with the plant''s name.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 122, 'Greet your host first at a summer barbecue before you head over to the snack table.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 123, 'Request the story behind a family recipe your host serves you, and listen for the names in it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 124, 'Share your plans for the day over breakfast so your host knows when to expect you back.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 125, 'Take one last look around the living room for your scarf, phone or glasses before you say goodbye.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 126, 'Wrap a small gift in brown paper and a bit of string, and draw a little leaf or flower in one corner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 127, 'Keep your voice soft if you arrive and hear a baby sleeping, and greet everyone in a near whisper.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 128, 'Take your plate into the kitchen at a potluck and ask where they would like it to go.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 129, 'Text your host if you will be home later than you said, so no one waits up or worries.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 130, 'Tell your host your departure time early on the last day of a stay, so they can plan their afternoon.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 131, 'Choose a host gift that asks nothing of your host, like a box of tea, rather than something they must arrange or cook.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 132, 'Plan a small, friendly first line to say at the door, like "It''s so good to see you," so arriving feels easier.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 133, 'Sweep the leaves tracked onto the porch during an autumn visit, once your host says it would help.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 134, 'Volunteer to walk the family dog one morning if your host would find that helpful.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 135, 'Write down three things you enjoyed about a visit while they are fresh, to use in a thank you note later.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 136, 'Set a gentle budget for a host gift before you shop, so a thoughtful choice never becomes a costly one.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 137, 'Notice the first friendly face you see when you walk in, and head toward it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 138, 'Shake out the picnic blanket and fold it with a friend after a summer lunch in their yard.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 139, 'In the fall, offer to rake leaves or sweep the porch with your host for half an hour.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 140, 'Choose a card with a seasonal picture, such as autumn leaves or spring blossoms, for your next thank you note.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 141, 'Fill a small jar with homemade granola for a host at a fall gathering, and tie the lid with a ribbon.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 142, 'Stamp the snow off your boots on the porch on a winter evening before you come inside.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 143, 'Play a quiet card game with the children at the kids'' table during a winter gathering, if their parents are glad of it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 144, 'Locate the spare toilet paper and soap on your first evening, so you never need to ask in a hurry.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 145, 'Tuck a small packet of tea in with a borrowed dish when you return it to its owner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 146, 'Copy a favorite family recipe onto a card to give your host along with a few homemade cookies.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 147, 'Leave your bag by the door or where your host suggests, rather than in the middle of the room.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 148, 'Read a picture book aloud when your host''s little one brings it to you, with their parent close by.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 149, 'Charge your phone and cables in the guest room instead of leaving them on shared counters.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 150, 'Call a host the day after a visit just to say how much you enjoyed being there.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 151, 'Put together a little bag of tea or cocoa packets for a winter visit, with a note that says "for a quiet evening."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 152, 'Ask your host, "Is there anything I should know about the house?" when you arrive for a weekend stay.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 153, 'Learn the name of everyone at the table and use each name once during the meal.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 154, 'On a spring weekend, offer to water the garden or the houseplants while your host runs errands.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 155, 'Remember the name of the host''s dog or cat and say goodbye to it too on your way out.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 156, 'Take a slow breath in and a longer breath out on the doorstep before you knock, and let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 157, 'Use coasters from the moment you sit down if you notice that the household uses them.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 158, 'Follow up when someone shares news with a question such as "What was the best part?"'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 159, 'Take short showers in the morning so others in the house have plenty of hot water.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 160, 'Help fold the extra chairs or carry the folding table back to the garage after a big summer party.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 161, 'Notice if a visit makes you nervous, and remind yourself that your host invited you because they want your company.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 162, 'Compliment one particular photo on the wall and ask your host the story behind it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 163, 'Pause for a breath before you answer, so the person speaking can finish their thought.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 164, 'Learn what time the household usually eats dinner and plan your outings around it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 165, 'Gather your own cups, napkins and paper plates into the trash before leaving a backyard picnic.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 166, 'Sit in the car or on a nearby bench for one minute before you go in, and feel your feet on the ground.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 167, 'Introduce your partner or friend to your host right away if they have not met before.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 168, 'Change the subject kindly if talk turns to someone who isn''t there to speak for themselves.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 169, 'Bring a small book or puzzle for quiet evenings so your host does not feel they must entertain you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 170, 'Wipe down the counter where you helped serve before heading home from a potluck.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 171, 'Hold a warm drink or a cool bottle of water on the way to a visit and let it steady your hands.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 172, 'Offer your name with a smile to the neighbor who joins the backyard barbecue, and ask their name back.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 173, 'Pass the bread basket along so it reaches the far end of the table before you take a second roll.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 174, 'Step outside for a short walk after lunch to give the household a little breathing room.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 175, 'Accept leftovers graciously if they are offered, and say how much you look forward to enjoying them.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 176, 'Think of two easy conversation topics before you go, such as a good book, a recent walk, or the season''s weather.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 177, 'Admire the garden on a summer evening visit by naming one flower or vegetable you notice.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 178, 'Serve the person beside you first when a dish comes your way, keeping the meal flowing.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 179, 'Save the Wi-Fi password the first time you hear it, so you do not need to interrupt your host later.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 180, 'Notice if your body feels tired after a long visit and give yourself permission to rest without guilt.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 181, 'Prepare one friendly question for your host, like "How did you find this neighborhood?" or "What have you been enjoying lately?"'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 182, 'Let the host''s dog calm down before you greet it, if it gets excited when you come in.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 183, 'Lay the breakfast table on a quiet morning during a weekend stay, using the dishes your host shows you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 184, 'Buy the ingredients for the meal you cook yourself, so your host''s pantry is not used up.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 185, 'Sit in your parked car for a quiet minute before you drive home, letting the chatter of the gathering settle.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 186, 'Remember one detail your host shared last time you spoke, so you can ask how it turned out.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 187, 'Skip petting an animal that walks away from you, and simply say a soft hello from where you are.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 188, 'Carry the holiday leftovers to the fridge with your host, then ask where the containers belong.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 189, 'Choose a simple dish you know well, like soup or pasta, for the meal you offer to make.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 190, 'Picture the host''s face when they read your thank you note, and let that warm feeling stay with you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 191, 'Choose a light story from your week to share at the table, something short that invites others to join in.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 192, 'Excuse yourself to a quiet room for a few minutes at a big family gathering if you need to reset, and tell someone where you are.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 193, 'Hum or sing along when the family gathers around the piano, even if you only know the chorus.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 194, 'Clean the pots and wipe the stove right after you cook, before you sit down to relax.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 195, 'Write a thank you note to a relative who hosted a holiday meal, naming the dish that reminded you of childhood.'),
