  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 205, 'Offer to take the trash or recycling out on your way to the car after a winter dinner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 206, 'Wear easy slip on shoes to a home where shoes come off, so you aren''t wrestling with laces in a narrow hallway.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 207, 'Follow the household''s lead on toasts or a moment of thanks before the meal, joining in as you feel comfortable.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 208, 'Accept a "No, you''re our guest" with a smile and simply enjoy being looked after.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 209, 'Empty the guest room wastebasket into the household trash on your last morning.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 210, 'Leave a small jar of jam or a fresh loaf for the household''s next breakfast as a parting thank you after an overnight stay.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 211, 'Tuck a pair of clean socks or soft slippers in your bag when you visit a home that keeps shoes at the door.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 212, 'Check what your host''s parents like to be called if you are meeting them for the first time.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 213, 'Chat with an aunt or uncle on the porch about what they''re looking forward to this spring.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 214, 'Open the guest room curtains each morning and leave the room looking bright and neat.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 215, 'Mention a specific kindness in your thank you, like the extra blanket they set out or the ride from the station.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 216, 'Tuck a small comb, lip balm or tissues in your pocket so you feel ready when you arrive.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 217, 'Greet the host''s kids by name when you arrive, and ask them one easy question about their day.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 218, 'Enjoy each bite of a dish your host is proud of, and let them know which part you liked best.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 219, 'Look under the bed and in every drawer for your belongings before you carry your bag out.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 220, 'Ask yourself on the way home what you''d like to do the same way the next time you visit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 221, 'Wipe your boots well on the mat on a muddy spring afternoon, and offer to leave them by the door.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 222, 'Bring a small story or photo to share if your host asked how your trip or new job is going.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 223, 'Leave room at the table for others to talk, aiming to listen a little more than you speak.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 224, 'Put the guest room chair, lamp and pillows back where they were when you arrived.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 225, 'Forgive yourself for a small slip, like spilling juice or forgetting a name, and remember your host has likely forgotten it already.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 226, 'Pack an umbrella and a small bag for wet shoes before a rainy fall visit, so you don''t track water inside.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 227, 'Text your host a quick "On my way" before a winter dinner so they know when to expect you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 228, 'Water the porch plants during a summer stay if your host mentions they need it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 229, 'Before an early start, find out whether a running shower or kettle might wake anyone in the house.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 230, 'Schedule a free evening after a weekend of visits, with nothing planned but rest.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 231, 'Make a short packing list for a weekend stay, including your own toiletries, a phone charger and comfortable clothes.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 232, 'Say a cheerful "Happy birthday!" to the birthday child first when you walk into a kids'' party.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 233, 'Fit a few pieces into the jigsaw puzzle on the coffee table during a rainy afternoon visit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 234, 'Keep phone calls short, and step outside or into the guest room to take them.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 235, 'Hug or wave goodbye, whichever feels comfortable for you and the people you are leaving.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 236, 'Learn the rhythm of the household before a weekend stay: roughly when everyone wakes up and when they head to bed.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 237, 'Hang back a moment in the doorway of a crowded holiday party until your host comes to greet you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 238, 'Ask your host''s teenager about a show or song they like, and listen without judgment.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 239, 'During a holiday visit, offer to run one errand, such as picking up bread or a forgotten ingredient.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 240, 'Bring an empty bag along so you can carry your own dish home after a potluck without fuss.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 241, 'Confirm your arrival and leaving times for an overnight stay, so your host knows when to expect you and when the room is free again.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 242, 'Mention one specific thing you appreciate about the table setting at a holiday meal.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 243, 'Let an older relative teach you a card game they loved, and play a round together.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 244, 'Leave the bathroom mirror and counter as clean as you found them before you head home.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 245, 'Return a borrowed book, umbrella or sweater from a recent visit with a quick thank you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 246, 'Ask whether you should bring your own towel or pillow for a weekend stay, rather than assuming either way.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 247, 'Find out where to put your dish or gift when you arrive, rather than setting it down anywhere.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 248, 'Thank whoever set the table, mentioning a detail you noticed, like the flowers or the candles.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 249, 'Ask who locks the door at night and what you should do if you come in after everyone is asleep.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 250, 'Stand up when you say you''re leaving, so a goodbye on a fall evening doesn''t stretch into another hour.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 251, 'Offer to bring something for breakfast on the second morning of a weekend stay, so your host has one less meal to plan.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 252, 'Wait to open the fridge or a cupboard in someone else''s kitchen until you have asked first.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 253, 'Share the load with someone as you carry a cooler from the car to the backyard at a summer cookout.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 254, 'Refill the water pitcher or ice tray whenever you are the one who empties it.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 255, 'Thank the host''s partner or family members by name, since hosting is often shared work.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 256, 'Read the invitation again the day before, and check the time, the address and anything you said you''d bring.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 257, 'Accept the seat your host offers at a backyard barbecue, even if it is not the shady spot you hoped for.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 258, 'Try "What''s one thing you''ve been enjoying lately?" when the conversation lulls at dinner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 259, 'Turn off the guest room lights and unplug your chargers whenever you head out for the day.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 260, 'Look around the table once before you leave and catch the eye of anyone you haven''t said goodbye to yet.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 261, 'Put the gift, your keys and anything you promised to bring by the front door the night before.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 262, 'Join the conversation already happening when you arrive, rather than starting a new topic right away.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 263, 'Turn toward your host and make eye contact while they tell you about their garden.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 264, 'Invite the children to a board game for an hour so their parents get a quiet rest.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 265, 'Leave a little earlier than planned on a snowy evening so your host isn''t worried about you on icy roads.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 266, 'Set a reminder an hour before you need to leave, so you can get ready without rushing.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 267, 'Unpack only what you need on the first evening of a weekend stay, keeping your things tidy in the guest room.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 268, 'Fetch an extra blanket for a relative who seems chilly on a winter evening.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 269, 'Ask your host for one thing they would like help with during your stay, then do it cheerfully.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 270, 'Unpack your bag soon after you get home, so the visit can settle into a happy memory.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 271, 'Pick comfortable, clean clothes that suit the setting, whether it''s a backyard barbecue or a holiday dinner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 272, 'Offer the host''s cat a slow blink from across the room and let it decide whether to come over.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 273, 'Gather the wrapping paper into a bag after gifts are opened at a holiday visit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 274, 'Let your host choose the TV shows and music, and ask before changing what is playing.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 275, 'Jot a small reminder in your calendar to invite your host back before the season ends.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 276, 'Text a quick question about what to wear, casual or a little dressy, so you can relax about your outfit.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 277, 'Sing along to the birthday song with gusto at a kids'' party, even if you are a little off key.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 278, 'Clap with real cheer when a child at a family gathering puts on a little dance show for you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 279, 'When rain keeps everyone in one afternoon, settle into a quiet corner with a book so the household can carry on as usual.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 280, 'Offer your host a date and a simple plan, like soup on a rainy autumn night, when you invite them over in return.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 281, 'Charge your phone before an evening visit, so finding your way home later feels easy.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 282, 'Say hello to whoever is working in the kitchen when you arrive, even if it is not the host.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 283, 'Ask the cook which dish they would make again, and why it is their favorite.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 284, 'Spend an hour exploring the neighborhood on foot so your host can nap or read in peace.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 285, 'Make your return invitation relaxed, such as a spring picnic, sandwiches on your porch or a board game afternoon.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 286, 'Check the forecast before a summer garden party, and bring a light layer or a sun hat to match the day.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 287, 'Remember one name from the introductions at a party and use it later in the evening.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 288, 'Pack a deck of cards in your bag to offer if the evening at a friend''s home grows quiet.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 289, 'Use the guest towels your host set out rather than reaching for the family''s own.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 290, 'Be honest with yourself about what felt hard during a visit, then name one thing that went well too.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 291, 'Bring a bottle of water and a small snack for a long trip to a relative''s home, so you arrive feeling steady.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 292, 'Rehearse a gentle way to step away, like "I''m going to get some fresh air," before a big gathering.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 293, 'Brush the crumbs from your place at the table onto your plate before you stand up.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 294, 'Pack a simple picnic lunch for everyone one summer afternoon so your host gets a break from the kitchen.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 295, 'Smile at the memory of a funny moment from a visit as you fall asleep tonight.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 296, 'Invite your host to mention anything you should know about the house, like a sleeping baby or a shy cat.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 297, 'Duck into a quiet hallway and sip some water if the noise at a birthday party gets to be a lot.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 298, 'Push in the chairs once everyone leaves the table after a long lunch.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 299, 'Check before inviting anyone else over or posting photos of your host''s home online.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 300, 'Close the guest room window, turn off the lamp and leave the door the way your host prefers before you go.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 301, 'Find out who else is coming to a gathering, so you can look forward to a few familiar faces.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 302, 'Tell your host one specific thing you love about their new apartment when you visit for the first time.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 303, 'Check how your host likes the dishwasher loaded before you add your plate.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 304, 'Air out the guest room for a few minutes on a mild spring morning, if your host is happy with that.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 305, 'Pack your bags the night before leaving a weekend stay, so the morning goodbye feels relaxed.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 306, 'Learn the names of your host''s partner and children before a visit, so you can greet each of them warmly.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 307, 'Look for the recycling bin, or check where it goes, before you toss anything in a friend''s kitchen.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 308, 'Let someone tell their story fully even when you have a similar one ready to share.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 309, 'Sweep or vacuum the guest room floor before you go, using whatever your host keeps handy.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 310, 'Give a neighbor or fellow guest a ride home if they are on your way and would like one.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 311, 'Ask a mutual friend how to pronounce your host''s name if you''re unsure, so your greeting feels easy.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 312, 'Wave hello to the neighbors chatting over the fence at a summer barbecue.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 313, 'Praise the cook''s effort, even for a simple spread of sandwiches at a spring picnic.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 314, 'Sort out bathroom turns on busy mornings by asking who needs to leave the house first.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 315, 'Say "I had a really good time" out loud at the door, even if you feel a little shy.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 316, 'Plan to arrive on time or a few minutes after, rather than early, so your host has a moment to finish getting ready.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 317, 'Match your host''s greeting, a hug or a handshake, and let them choose what feels comfortable.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 318, 'Arrange crackers on a plate or toss the salad when your host is busy at the stove.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 319, 'Tell your host right away about anything you spilled or broke, and offer to set it right.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 320, 'Give your host a moment to rest at the end of a party by saying a quick goodbye instead of starting a new topic.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 321, 'Decide how long you''ll stay at a casual afternoon visit, and mention it kindly so your host isn''t left wondering.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 322, 'Admire the season''s touches on your host''s porch, like a wreath or pumpkins, as you come up the steps.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 323, 'Join a gentle backyard game of catch or croquet at an autumn family gathering.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 324, 'Set the table for the family''s holiday meal so the cook can focus on the kitchen.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 325, 'Wrap up a conversation gently at the door with, "Let''s pick this up next time," and head out with a wave.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 326, 'Tell your host when you reply if you''ll need to leave early, so it doesn''t come as a surprise later.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 327, 'Welcome a guest who arrives after you by introducing yourself and showing them where the coats go.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 328, 'Choose the youngest guest as your partner in a simple game, with their parent''s okay.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 329, 'Help clear the table after a big holiday dinner, then follow how your host likes the dishes done.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 330, 'Rest your feet for a few minutes when you get home from a long summer afternoon at someone''s house.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 331, 'Confirm with a relative whether gifts are part of a holiday gathering, since some families like to keep it simple.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 332, 'Hold off on asking for a house tour until your host offers one, and enjoy the room you are in.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 333, 'Offer to make the coffee or tea after dinner if your host shows you where things are.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 334, 'Keep the guest room window shut on cold winter days so the warmth stays inside the house.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 335, 'Let a minor misunderstanding from a visit go, and trust that the friendship is bigger than one moment.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 336, 'Make a simple homemade card with a pressed flower or a doodle, ready to hand over at the door.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 337, 'Listen for whether people speak quietly or loudly in this home, and match the household''s volume.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 338, 'Answer questions about yourself briefly, then turn the conversation back with "And how about you?"'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 339, 'Set the guest room door open or closed while you are out, whichever your host prefers.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 340, 'Remind yourself as you put on your shoes that leaving on time is a kindness, not a rejection.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 341, 'Picture the moment the door opens, and plan your first words: a hello, a smile, and "Thank you for having me."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 342, 'Compliment the music playing when you settle in at a friend''s place on a fall afternoon.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 343, 'Swap a heated topic at the table for a light, happy memory everyone can enjoy.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 344, 'Learn any pet routines, like feeding times, so you do not accidentally give the animals extra food.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 345, 'Choose a quiet activity for the evening after visiting family, like a warm bath, a puzzle or an early night.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 346, 'Keep a small stack of blank cards at home, so one is always ready to tuck into a host gift.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 347, 'Ask the youngest guest at a family dinner a friendly question so they feel included.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 348, 'Take the trash or recycling out after a big family meal, following your host''s lead on where it goes.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 349, 'Let your host know if you plan to sleep in, so they do not hold breakfast for you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 350, 'Hold the door for the next guest leaving as you head out together.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 351, 'Double check whether to use the front door or the side gate for a spring garden lunch, so you arrive at the right step.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 352, 'Charge your phone in the spot your host suggests during a weekend stay, and leave it there through dinner.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 353, 'Spread a tablecloth with your host for a spring brunch, smoothing out the corners together.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 354, 'Leave a short handwritten thank you note on the made bed when you leave.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 355, 'Share a kind word about the visit with someone else, like "Aunt Rosa makes the coziest home."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 356, 'Call your host for a quick chat about the plan for the day, such as a meal, a walk or games, so you can come prepared.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 357, 'Relax into your host''s plan for the evening by saying, "Whatever you had in mind sounds great."'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 358, 'Keep an older relative company for a little while when they''re resting in a quieter room.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 359, 'Return the spare house key into your host''s hand before you go, rather than leaving it on a table.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 360, 'Address and stamp your thank you note right away so it goes out with the next mail pickup.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 361, 'Reply to a group invitation right in the thread, so your host doesn''t have to chase your answer.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 362, 'Bring a light sweater to a spring garden visit so you can stay comfortable wherever your host seats you.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 363, 'Savor a warm drink your host makes you on a cold morning and tell them how nice it is.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 364, 'Send a message once you get home saying you arrived safely and naming one moment you enjoyed.'),
  ('being-a-thoughtful-guest', 365, 'Appreciate yourself for showing up, helping out and saying thank you, whether the visit felt smooth or a bit bumpy.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
